---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Deathwatch Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Deathwatch? Learn how this elite xenos-hunting force plays, how to paint their iconic black armor, and exactly what to buy first."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🌑</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Deathwatch</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            Not a Chapter — a vigil. Warriors plucked from every Space Marine Chapter across
            the galaxy, united in black armor with a single mission: hunt and eliminate xenos
            threats too dangerous for anyone else to face.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Elite Kill Teams</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Deathwatch?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          The Deathwatch is not a Chapter in the traditional sense. You won't find a Deathwatch
          homeworld or recruitment program. Instead, they are warriors — sometimes one, sometimes
          a handful — seconded from other Chapters throughout the Imperium. A Blood Angel.
          An Ultramarine. A Space Wolf. A Dark Angel. Each answers the call at different times
          in their career, and each brings something the others don't.
        </p>
        <p>
          They operate under the aegis of the Inquisition's Ordo Xenos — the branch tasked
          with studying and eliminating alien threats. Where regular Imperial forces deal with
          xenos armies by the regiment, the Deathwatch deals with them by the kill team. Their
          purpose is precision: find the critical target, eliminate it, vanish. A Deathwatch kill
          team can take out the synapse creature that coordinates a Tyranid swarm, or destroy the
          psychic beacon that guides an Ork Waaagh! before it reaches full force.
        </p>
        <p>
          The visual identity tells the whole story. Each Deathwatch warrior repaints one
          shoulder pad — the left — in black with the silver Deathwatch Chapter symbol.
          The right shoulder pad remains in their home Chapter's colors. A squad could have
          a blue Ultramarine pad, a red Blood Angel pad, a grey Space Wolf pad, all on
          warriors standing shoulder to shoulder. It's an immediately recognizable aesthetic
          unlike anything else in the game.
        </p>
        <p>
          After their service, warriors return to their Chapters — changed. The Deathwatch
          is a crucible. Those who survive it come back as something more.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Deathwatch excel at building <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">specialized Kill Teams</strong>
          — small squads of mixed specialists kitted out to handle a specific threat. Their core
          ability: access to a massive variety of weapons tuned against specific xenos types.
          Anti-infantry weapons for hordes, anti-armor for vehicles and monstrous creatures,
          psych-out grenades for psychic opponents. The army rewards players who do their homework
          on the meta.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Combat Patrol gives you Primaris marines — specifically Intercessors, Aggressors,
          and a Lieutenant and Apothecary as leaders — along with Deathwatch Upgrade Frames
          that add the signature visual identity (Deathwatch pads, accessories, alternate weapons).
          This is a solid core: durable, flexible, and capable of both shooting and melee.
        </p>
        <p>
          The complexity comes from knowing what you're fighting. Deathwatch players ideally
          want to tune their squads before each game based on the opponent. In casual play this
          is satisfying puzzle-solving. In competitive play it's a significant depth advantage.
          The army is medium difficulty to learn but has high mastery potential.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Deathwatch are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love collecting models from multiple Chapters</li>
            <li>✓ You want flexible, specialized gameplay</li>
            <li>✓ You love the black armor + multi-color pauldron aesthetic</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy adapting your list to the opponent</li>
            <li>✓ You want Inquisition-flavored secretive operatives</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You want to bring the same list every game</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer simple, straightforward army rules</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde army with many cheap models</li>
            <li>✗ You'd rather not think about your opponent's faction</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Deathwatch</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Black armor is actually one of the easiest schemes in the hobby. The real artistry
        is in the Chapter-colored shoulder pads — and that's where you get to show off.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray with Abaddon Black (or black primer)</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Cover the entire model. The black spray IS your base coat and your armor color — no second pass needed. This is why black armor is beginner-friendly.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Drybrush edges with Thunderhawk Blue or Eshin Grey</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Load a large brush with paint, wipe most of it off, then lightly scrub across every edge and raised surface. This creates the illusion of light hitting the black armor without any careful brushwork.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint the left (Deathwatch) shoulder pad</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Leave it black — it already is. Paint the silver Deathwatch symbol with Leadbelcher or Ironbreaker. This is the iconic detail that ties every warrior together.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint the right (Chapter) shoulder pad in Chapter colors</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Each warrior gets their home Chapter's color here. Blue for Ultramarines, red for Blood Angels, grey for Space Wolves. Pick a consistent set of Chapters for your Kill Teams — three or four creates beautiful visual variety without chaos.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Silver and gold trim details</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Leadbelcher on the bolter casing and any metallic details. Retributor Armour on the chest eagle and any gold ornaments. Red dot on eye lenses.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Base the model</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Astrogranite Debris texture paint, drybrush Administratum Grey, add a tuft. The stark black armor pops even more against a textured grey-brown base.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tip box -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The Chapter pad strategy</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Pick 3–4 Chapters you want to represent in your force and paint one or two warriors
          from each. The visual contrast between all-black armor and bright colored pads is
          the entire aesthetic of Deathwatch — lean into it. It's also a great excuse to
          try painting a few different Chapter schemes without committing to a whole army of each.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. Paint it before buying anything else.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Deathwatch</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Includes 1x Primaris Lieutenant, 1x Primaris Apothecary, 10x Primaris Intercessors,
          3x Primaris Aggressors, and 2x Deathwatch Upgrade Frames. The upgrade frames
          are what transform standard Primaris marines into visual Deathwatch — Deathwatch
          shoulder pads, specialized weapons, and Inquisition-flavored accessories.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The Apothecary is a fantastic support character that keeps your elite warriors
          alive. The Aggressors are close-range powerhouses. Together it's a well-rounded
          kill team ready to hunt xenos.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=combat+patrol+deathwatch+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon for Combat Patrol →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$55 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Deathwatch Kill Team</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The dedicated Deathwatch veteran marines kit — includes special weapons, bespoke
          Deathwatch upgrades, and the parts to build a true mixed-Chapter kill team.
          This is the box that lets you play the faction as intended, mixing specialist load-outs.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=deathwatch+kill+team+veterans+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Black Spray (Chaos Black or equivalent)', use: 'Base coat — armor color done instantly', required: true },
            { name: 'Thunderhawk Blue or Eshin Grey', use: 'Drybrush for edge definition on black armor', required: true },
            { name: 'Leadbelcher / Ironbreaker', use: 'Silver Deathwatch symbol and metallic trim', required: true },
            { name: 'Retributor Armour', use: 'Gold chest eagle and ornaments', required: true },
            { name: 'Chapter colors (your choice)', use: 'Right shoulder pad — pick 3–4 Chapters', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade on silver and gold areas', required: false },
            { name: 'Mephiston Red', use: 'Eye lenses', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">You'll need a few extra pots for whichever Chapters you choose to represent — but it's a small investment for big visual payoff.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Deathwatch', cost: '~$160', note: 'Lieutenant, Apothecary, Intercessors, Aggressors + upgrade frames' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (5)', cost: '~$30', note: 'Black spray + drybrush color + silvers + gold' },
          { item: 'Chapter pad paints (3–4 extra)', cost: '~$15', note: 'A pot or two per Chapter you represent' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Or plastic glue — both work' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$242</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Prices approximate. Black armor is actually the most budget-friendly scheme — you
        spend more on variety than on volumes of paint. The upgrade frames are the critical
        purchase to nail the Deathwatch aesthetic.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">The vigil never ends.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        Somewhere out there, xenos are massing. The Deathwatch are already on their way.
        Grab the Combat Patrol, pick your three favorite Chapters to represent, and begin
        your service.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
